From: UniXNU contributors
Subject: [PATCH] k60: link the generated ADSP carrier blob

The ADSP firmware travels inside the kernel as an .incbin assembly file
(P-197: the firmware volume has no loader). Name the generated file in
osfmk/conf/files.arm64 so the kernel build assembles and links it,
exactly like the Metal plugin blob in 0610. The file is generated by
build-xnu-4k-baseline.sh only when K60_ADSP_BLOB_S is set; a build
without --adsp-blob has no such file and the entry is inert, the same
way a missing optional source is tolerated elsewhere in this list.
diff --git a/osfmk/conf/files.arm64 b/osfmk/conf/files.arm64
--- a/osfmk/conf/files.arm64
+++ b/osfmk/conf/files.arm64
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 osfmk/arm64/WKdmCompress_16k.s		standard
 osfmk/arm64/WKdmDecompress_4k.s	standard
 osfmk/arm64/k60_metal_blob.s	standard
+osfmk/arm64/k60_adsp_blob.s	standard
 osfmk/arm64/WKdmCompress_4k.s	standard
 osfmk/arm64/WKdmData.s		standard
 osfmk/arm64/lz4_decode_arm64.s  standard
